module lib/random
  Random draws, each a formula over the built-in generator `rand()`, so every
  engine draws the same numbers from the same seed.

randn  @6c0c651f
  what  A standard normal draw: Box-Muller's cosine branch, u1 drawn before u2.
  u1    the first uniform draw, in (0, 1)
  u2    the second

randn_matrix  @d1c0afa6
  what  A `rows` by `cols` matrix of standard normal draws, filled row by row.
  rows  the rows
  cols  the columns
  Z     the matrix
  i     a row
  j     a column

randint  @6eab3eae
  what  An integer drawn uniformly from `lo`, `lo + 1`, ..., `hi - 1`.

arange  @91dcd145
  what  `[0, 1, ..., n - 1]`.

shuffle  @527cf2f8
  what  Shuffle a 1-D array in place: Fisher-Yates from the top index down.

randperm  @7f098ba5
  what  A random ordering of `0, 1, ..., n - 1` (torch.randperm).

choice  @0c7c205a
  what  An index drawn with the probabilities `p`, by inverting the cumulative sum at
        one uniform draw (torch.multinomial with one sample).
  why   Index k is returned when the draw lands in the k-th stretch of the unit
        interval, and that stretch is `p[k]` long.
  p     the probabilities, one per index, summing to one
  u     the uniform draw
  cum   the probabilities summed up to and including index k
  k     an index
